WEBVTT

00:00:01.960 --> 00:00:05.870
Tight matches continue here at the 
National Vanguard Championship,

00:00:05.870 --> 00:00:08.300
but now the preliminary 
blocks break for lunch.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.370
Fighters, take a brief respite of peace!

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:12.910
Fill up with a nutritious lunch

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:15.870
so you can wow us with more 
passionate fights this afternoon!

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:18.070
Huh? Dr. O?

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:19.740
Did you already go to lunch?

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.090
I thought we'd go together...

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:26.400
Two elimination fights are over, 
and AL4 won both of theirs.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:30.000
Q4 and the Jurassic Army each 
have one win and one loss.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.190
To make it past the elimination round, 
we have to win our next fight.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:38.040
That way, Kamui can come back to the team

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.270
and we can fight in the finals together!

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.560
Brother...

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.250
Aichi, you talk like that, but do you 
know who you're up against next?!

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:52.400
Yep. Team AL4. Last year's winning team...

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:54.360
Y-You...

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.470
Do you really think you're gonna win?

00:00:57.620 --> 00:00:59.390
We may not win...

00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:04.130
But I want to!

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:07.190
That's the spirit!

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:09.580
But that's why he's my number one disciple!

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:12.980
Do you have a chance of winning?

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:15.380
I just fight my own match.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:23.080
You guys make me laugh.

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:24.250
Yeah, really.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.650
You... beat us? Seriously?

00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:28.410
AL4...

00:03:06.590 --> 00:03:11.660
Your first time here and you think 
you can win against us, AL4?

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:13.750
What nonsense!

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.450
W-We'll see when we fight!

00:03:16.450 --> 00:03:17.910
Clam it, little fish!

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:19.940
Why, you...!

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:21.600
M-Morikawa!

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.400
I guess little fish hang out with each 
other, huh, in the little fish river!

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.260
What was that, you...?!

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:29.910
Tetsu, where's Ren?

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:34.480
Like I said before, he's not participating 
in the elimination round.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:38.990
For Ren, playing in the elimination 
round isn't worth the bother.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:40.790
We can handle it on our own.

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:43.760
Are you so interested in Ren

00:03:43.760 --> 00:03:46.670
because the two of you were 
once on the same team?

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.450
Kai, is that true?

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:55.540
Ren, Ren, Ren...

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:57.780
What's so great about him?

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:00.090
Kyou, a little respect for Ren...

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:01.500
He is our leader.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.130
Oh, shut up, Asaka! I can say what I want!

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:07.240
I don't like this guy! All he sees is Ren!

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:09.790
I'm gonna crush you!

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:13.130
Are you listening to me?!

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:16.210
I hear you and Ren are evenly matched...

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:20.120
So, if I defeat you, it 
means I'm stronger than Ren!

00:04:20.390 --> 00:04:22.570
I'll be the leader of AL4!

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:25.200
Kyou, do you know what you're saying?

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:28.400
Sure! The guy with the most 
ability should stand at the top!

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:29.060
Kyou!

00:04:29.060 --> 00:04:30.080
That's enough.

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:34.900
At any rate, you can't beat us.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.600
We'll prove it to you in our fight.

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:37.450
Let's go.

00:04:39.030 --> 00:04:40.220
Go on, get outta here!

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:41.920
Morikawa...

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:43.850
Ren and Kai once...?

00:04:45.270 --> 00:04:46.200
Kai!

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:51.650
Well, until he wants to talk about it,

00:04:51.650 --> 00:04:53.870
we should leave it alone.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:55.260
Aichi!

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:57.440
Emi!

00:04:58.100 --> 00:04:59.610
Miss Emi!

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:01.890
I brought you some lunch...

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:04.050
but maybe not in this place?

00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:05.700
Y-Yeah, actually...

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:06.800
I see...

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:11.140
But we'll all feast on it 
later, so okay, no problem!

00:05:11.140 --> 00:05:12.140
Right!

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:14.510
If only the great Kamui were here...

00:05:14.990 --> 00:05:16.910
The sandwich she made 
last time was delicious!

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:19.670
Miss Emi's homemade lunch...

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:21.420
Kamui, where are you?!

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:25.330
Oh, Nagisa and Gouki!

00:05:25.330 --> 00:05:26.140
Yo!

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:29.890
We're here to cheer you guys on. Looks 
like you're hangin' in there, huh?

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:32.860
Y-Yes! Thank you!

00:05:32.860 --> 00:05:36.590
Where's Kamui? His beloved 
made a lunch just for him!

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:39.190
A-Actually, nobody knows where he is...

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.760
NK, yo!

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:43.330
Kamui, where are you?!

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.230
I'm sorry, Miss Emi!

00:05:45.230 --> 00:05:47.640
Once again, I can't eat your lunch!

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:50.880
Kamui!!

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:56.420
Kai...

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:06.070
Ren...

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:12.140
The Strongest Team, AL4!

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.380
We thought you would not be coming 
to the elimination rounds,

00:06:23.380 --> 00:06:24.430
Ren...

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:28.960
How's it going?

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:31.870
We won our first two fights, 
and there's one remaining.

00:06:33.010 --> 00:06:34.180
Anything else?

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:36.350
Um... The next team we're up against...

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:39.170
Nothing. Everything is fine.

00:06:43.220 --> 00:06:44.410
I see.

00:06:48.950 --> 00:06:52.170
Tetsu, why didn't you say anything about Kai?

00:06:54.530 --> 00:06:57.200
The silent treatment, huh? Jerk...

00:06:58.540 --> 00:07:01.270
All right, lunch break is over!

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:02.840
The elimination round resumes!

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:04.590
The play-by-play is by me, MC Miya!

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:07.600
Plus commentary by me, Dr. O! Thank you!

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:08.930
Elimination round, A Block,

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:12.130
Team AL4 versus Team Q4!

00:07:12.130 --> 00:07:13.890
What are the key points here?

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:16.070
AL4 is the winning team from last year,

00:07:16.070 --> 00:07:21.270
and in this elimination round, 
they've won all of their matches.

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:24.770
How far can Q4, making their 
debut here, go against them?

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:25.750
That's the question.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:29.090
We have to win!

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:33.590
My cheering is the strongest here!

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:35.970
Thanks to that, you guys 
won't lose, so relax!

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.610
That's cheering?

00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:39.590
He sure loves his "strongest"...

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:42.930
Kamui, where are you?!

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.760
I'm really sorry...

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:46.380
RS, yo!

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:51.710
The first match! Yahagi Kyou of 
AL4 versus Kai Toshiki of Team Q4!

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:55.120
Kai...

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:58.770
I see. So he's here...

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:03.060
Tetsu, pretense was uncalled for...

00:08:03.390 --> 00:08:06.490
Ren is preoccupied with Kai.

00:08:06.490 --> 00:08:09.250
No... "hates him" is more accurate...

00:08:09.590 --> 00:08:12.250
That's exactly why I couldn't let him know...

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:21.170
Beating you will prove that Crusher 
Kyou is the strongest member of AL4!

00:08:21.900 --> 00:08:24.150
I see. He's here...

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:38.490
Knock it off! I'm your opponent!

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.380
Judge! Anytime you're ready!

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:42.590
Begin the match!

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:45.520
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:08:43.030 --> 00:08:45.520
Stand up the Vanguard!

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:54.770
I ride Embodiment of Armor, Bahr!

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:57.300
I move Conroe!

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:59.460
The enemy has a Spike Brothers deck, huh?

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:02.250
That's the playing field of 
Juggernaut Maximum, right?

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:03.900
I see... That's right!

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:05.430
He was slow to pick up on it...

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:08.500
The Great Kyou rides Wonder Boy!

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:12.740
That's Kamui's catchphrase!

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:16.250
Take this!

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:22.670
I ride Dragon Knight, Nehalem!

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:27.290
I move Conroe to the front.

00:09:27.290 --> 00:09:30.820
Then I call Demonic Dragon Mage, 
Kimnara and Blazing Core Dragon!

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:33.350
I attack with Blazing Core!

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:36.990
I attack with Nehalem!

00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:43.060
I attack with Conroe, boosted by Kimnara!

00:09:43.410 --> 00:09:46.260
I guard with Spike Brothers Assault Squad!

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:50.920
Turn end!

00:09:51.890 --> 00:09:54.840
The Great Kyou rides Treasured Black Panther!

00:09:58.690 --> 00:10:01.810
I call Highspeed, Brakki and Devil Summoner!

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:03.650
I activate Summoner's skill!

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:07.690
I flip over the top card of my deck, and 
if it's a grade 1 or 2 Spike Brothers,

00:10:07.690 --> 00:10:09.330
I can do a superior call!

00:10:09.330 --> 00:10:11.540
I superior call Assault Squad!

00:10:12.710 --> 00:10:14.430
Superior call!

00:10:14.430 --> 00:10:17.010
SC! That's a superior pain!

00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:20.620
I attack with Brakki, 
boosted by Assault Squad!

00:10:24.380 --> 00:10:26.170
I attack with Panther!

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:30.320
With a boost from Mecha Trainer...

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:31.810
Summoner attacks!

00:10:32.930 --> 00:10:34.350
I guard with Tahr.

00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:39.470
That's the end of my turn.

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:45.270
It's a quiet build-up...

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:46.370
They're tied, huh?

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:47.120
Uh huh.

00:10:47.700 --> 00:10:51.000
But why do I feel so anxious?

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:06.220
Picture it...

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:08.850
This is my true form!

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:10.580
Ride the Vanguard!

00:11:12.350 --> 00:11:15.940
The apocalyptic flames that reduce 
everything in this world to ashes!

00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:18.510
Dragonic Overlord!

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:26.250
I call Dual Axe Archdragon.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:29.050
Overlord's Counterblast!

00:11:32.990 --> 00:11:35.820
There it is! The pattern that 
always leads Kai to victory!

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:37.200
That's +5000 power!

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:38.070
All right!

00:11:38.070 --> 00:11:40.090
He'll lose the twin drive skill,

00:11:40.090 --> 00:11:43.300
but when an attack hits the 
rear-guard, Overlord stands!

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:44.740
He's just as good as won!

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:48.350
With a boost from Bahr...

00:11:48.350 --> 00:11:50.150
Overlord attacks!

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:06.340
Eternal flame!

00:12:11.350 --> 00:12:15.320
I guard with Silence Joker, Cheer 
Girl, Tiara, and Dudley Dan!

00:12:17.060 --> 00:12:18.940
He's guarding with three units?!

00:12:18.940 --> 00:12:22.400
I see! So even if he draws a critical 
trigger, it'll protect against that!

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:24.970
Check the drive trigger.

00:12:25.790 --> 00:12:28.570
Critical trigger...

00:12:28.570 --> 00:12:30.950
But even if I use it on Overlord, 
the attack will fall short...

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:36.120
I put the whole effect on Archdragon!

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:41.680
I don't believe it! His winning 
pattern was just torn down!

00:12:47.970 --> 00:12:50.500
That was your trump card, wasn't it?

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:53.360
But its skill requires a cost of 3...

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:57.240
Since you'll lose if you take 6 damage, 
you won't be able to do that again!

00:13:00.310 --> 00:13:02.890
This is what my bad feeling was about...

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:05.260
When Kyou was attacked three times,

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:07.430
he chose to guard in order to 
prevent losing his rear-guards,

00:13:07.430 --> 00:13:10.450
and Kai from drawing three triggers.

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:13.680
Even though he used a lot 
of cards from his hand,

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.650
it's a big deal that the 
attack didn't go through...

00:13:16.650 --> 00:13:18.470
Come and get me!

00:13:18.470 --> 00:13:21.570
Blazing Core attacks Brakki!

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.170
I intercept with Summoner!

00:13:27.890 --> 00:13:29.760
He protected the rear-guard?

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:32.410
To ensure that a superior 
unit stays on the field!

00:13:32.580 --> 00:13:34.140
With a boost from Kimnara,

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:35.850
Archdragon attacks!

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:42.360
Damage trigger check!

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:45.160
Draw trigger!

00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:49.890
It's my turn! Here I go with Crush Rush!

00:13:49.890 --> 00:13:50.960
Crush...

00:13:50.960 --> 00:13:51.830
...Rush?

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:53.960
Kai! Be careful! Here it comes!

00:13:57.050 --> 00:13:58.550
Here's my destroying rush!

00:13:58.550 --> 00:14:00.480
The sky is my field!

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.830
The Great Kyou rides Sky Diver!

00:14:06.430 --> 00:14:08.960
Mecha Trainer's Counterblast!

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:11.800
With that, I can look for 
any one grade 1 or less

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:14.530
Spike Brothers in my deck 
and add it to my hand!

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:16.890
I call Dudley Dan!

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:20.210
He called something!

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:23.580
I attack with Sky Diver, 
boosted by Dudley Dan!

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:27.620
Then I activate Dan's Counterblast!

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:30.940
By putting one Spike Brothers 
card into the Soul,

00:14:30.940 --> 00:14:33.920
I can superior call a Spike 
Brothers from my deck!

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:40.260
Another unit?! What the heck is he doing?!

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:42.860
This right here is Spike 
Brothers at its best!

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:46.590
I get it! Like an American football team,

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:50.060
one professional after another is called 
out onto the field for each position,

00:14:50.060 --> 00:14:55.060
and while the players are being subbed 
in and out, the team attacks in waves!

00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.650
Drive trigger check!

00:14:58.820 --> 00:14:59.950
First card...

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:01.070
Second card...

00:15:02.050 --> 00:15:03.530
Draw trigger!

00:15:03.530 --> 00:15:06.440
I give the power to Sky Diver, 
who hasn't attacked yet.

00:15:06.440 --> 00:15:07.780
And then I draw!

00:15:09.260 --> 00:15:11.160
With a boost from Assault Squad...

00:15:11.160 --> 00:15:12.590
Brakki attacks!

00:15:13.470 --> 00:15:15.790
I guard with Blu-ray Dracokid!

00:15:15.790 --> 00:15:17.700
I attack with Sky Diver!

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:20.970
Bloody Skydive that breaks 
through all defenses!

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:26.880
He held on...

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:30.040
It's still too early to relax...

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:32.060
I activate Sky Diver's skill!

00:15:32.060 --> 00:15:35.860
When an attack hits, if I 
put this unit into the Soul,

00:15:35.860 --> 00:15:39.860
I can superior call a Spike 
Brothers unit that's in my hand!

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:41.070
This guy!

00:15:43.810 --> 00:15:46.790
And now I can attack one more time!

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:52.480
This is the power of Crusher Kyou, who 
leaves not even a blade of grass standing!

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:54.190
Go, Sky Diver!

00:15:54.190 --> 00:15:55.930
Bloody Skydive!

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.080
I guard with Tahr!

00:15:58.730 --> 00:16:00.350
That's the end of my turn...

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:04.500
Yikes! Somehow, Kai managed to squeak by!

00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.410
If he doesn't seal the deal this 
turn, he'll be in deep trouble!

00:16:06.410 --> 00:16:08.170
But how many cards are in Kai's hand?

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:08.870
Zero!

00:16:08.870 --> 00:16:10.780
I stand and draw!

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:13.310
I attack Brakki with Blazing Core!

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:19.140
I'm chafin' here.

00:16:19.140 --> 00:16:20.690
The end of the match, and all he can do

00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:23.210
is aim for the rear-guard 'cause 
he doesn't have enough power...

00:16:23.440 --> 00:16:26.640
I attack with Overlord, boosted by Bahr!

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:32.050
I guard with Cheer Girl, Marilyn!

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:35.450
By dropping one Spike 
Brothers card from my hand,

00:16:35.450 --> 00:16:37.240
I can defend completely!

00:16:37.240 --> 00:16:39.120
Check the drive trigger.

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:43.070
Heal trigger.

00:16:43.070 --> 00:16:46.800
I add +5000 to the power of 
Archdragon and heal 1 damage!

00:16:47.770 --> 00:16:49.250
With a boost from Kimnara,

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:50.930
Archdragon attacks!

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:58.050
Damage trigger check...

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:02.300
Now it's my turn...

00:17:03.360 --> 00:17:05.050
Final Turn!

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:15.260
That's what you and Ren say, isn't it?

00:17:15.260 --> 00:17:17.910
Here I go! With a boost from Dudley Dan...

00:17:17.910 --> 00:17:21.160
Sky Diver attacks! And... Counterblast!

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:23.720
From my deck, I superior call...

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:25.440
Juggernaut Maximum!

00:17:28.210 --> 00:17:30.110
Are you serious?! It's all over!

00:17:30.110 --> 00:17:31.270
Could it be over...?

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:33.510
In a showdown, you won't 
know till the very end.

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:38.130
I guard with Dragon Monk, Genjo!

00:17:38.130 --> 00:17:39.880
Drive trigger check!

00:17:40.400 --> 00:17:42.120
Critical trigger!

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:44.170
I give all the effects to Juggernaut!

00:17:44.170 --> 00:17:46.380
And then Juggernaut attacks...

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:48.210
Assault Squad, give him a boost!

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.640
Juggernaut's Soulblast!

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:56.360
By dropping one card from the 
Soul, he gains +5000 power!

00:17:58.060 --> 00:17:59.400
I guard with Tahr!

00:17:59.400 --> 00:18:01.690
And on top of that, I 
intercept with Blazing Core!

00:18:04.660 --> 00:18:06.930
He doesn't know when to give up!

00:18:06.930 --> 00:18:08.720
Juggernaut goes back into the deck.

00:18:08.720 --> 00:18:10.380
I attack with Sky Diver!

00:18:10.700 --> 00:18:12.680
If he can get past this attack...

00:18:12.680 --> 00:18:14.320
It's too early to tell...

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:18.820
No guard.

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:22.890
Why?! If he's hit with Sky Diver's attack...

00:18:24.510 --> 00:18:26.380
He's going for broke! Kai...

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:31.300
I activate Sky Diver's skill!

00:18:31.300 --> 00:18:34.000
Sky Diver moves to the Soul. And then...

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:35.900
Panther wouldn't be able to reach him...

00:18:35.900 --> 00:18:36.980
In this instance...

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:39.700
Superior call! Devil Summoner!

00:18:40.130 --> 00:18:41.700
What's the top card of my deck?

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.740
There it is! I superior call Brakki!

00:18:46.510 --> 00:18:48.250
I attack with Brakki!

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:49.640
Soulblast!

00:18:49.640 --> 00:18:54.070
When Brakki attacks, dropping a card 
from the Soul gives him +5000 power!

00:18:55.240 --> 00:18:57.440
I guard with Iron Tail Dragon!

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:00.720
Brakki returns to my deck!

00:19:00.720 --> 00:19:02.040
That's the end of my turn!

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:04.500
Asaka. Get ready.

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:06.790
Final Turn!

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:11.300
Why do you think I let myself 
be attacked by Sky Diver?

00:19:11.300 --> 00:19:12.190
Why...?

00:19:13.110 --> 00:19:15.160
You have 3 cards face up in the damage zone.

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:21.930
Heal trigger! I heal 1 damage!

00:19:23.210 --> 00:19:24.540
No guard.

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:31.610
He recovered with a heal trigger...

00:19:31.610 --> 00:19:34.860
and willingly took damage so that three 
cards would be face-up in the damage zone!

00:19:35.180 --> 00:19:38.230
Dragonic Overlord's Counterblast!

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:41.710
With a boost from Bahr...

00:19:41.710 --> 00:19:44.230
Overlord attacks your Devil Summoner!

00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:45.600
Drive check!

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:47.180
Eternal Flame!

00:19:51.860 --> 00:19:54.380
Every time his attack hits the rear-guard,

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:56.980
Overlord stands!

00:19:57.650 --> 00:20:00.370
D-Don't tell me...

00:20:00.980 --> 00:20:02.180
I'm going to lose?!

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:05.510
Overlord attacks your Vanguard!

00:20:06.180 --> 00:20:09.520
I guard with Sonic Breaker and Black Panther!

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:11.110
Drive trigger check.

00:20:11.500 --> 00:20:13.010
With a boost from Kimnara...

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:14.710
Archdragon attacks!

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:17.900
If the opponent has two or fewer units in 
the rear-guard when Archdragon attacks,

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:19.490
it receives +3000 power!

00:20:21.920 --> 00:20:24.090
I-I'm going to... lose!

00:20:35.680 --> 00:20:36.800
I lost!

00:20:37.650 --> 00:20:41.790
The winner of the first match, 
Kai Toshiki of Team Q4!

00:20:42.330 --> 00:20:44.880
This can't be...

00:20:45.260 --> 00:20:47.930
Team Q4 won the match!

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:52.880
Team AL4 has suffered their first loss of this 
year's tournament, during the elimination round!

00:20:54.370 --> 00:20:55.820
Naturally...

00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:11.350
And now, let's move on to the second match!

00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:13.740
From Team AL4, Narumi Asaka!

00:21:13.740 --> 00:21:16.240
From Team Q4, Tokura Misaki!

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:22.790
Nice fight.

00:21:26.090 --> 00:21:27.400
Great job.

00:21:27.400 --> 00:21:29.090
That was awesome, Kai!

00:21:29.090 --> 00:21:31.060
Concentrate on your own match.

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:32.770
Okay...

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:34.690
Good luck, Misaki!

00:21:43.150 --> 00:21:44.900
The fight has only just begun...

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:48.120
There's no doubt that one of them 
is stronger than the guy I fought!

00:21:51.900 --> 00:21:55.300
The second match, Narumi 
Asaka versus Tokura Misaki!

00:21:57.160 --> 00:21:58.520
I'll tell you one thing.

00:21:58.520 --> 00:22:00.670
You won't beat me.

00:22:00.670 --> 00:22:02.260
Not with that deck.

00:23:52.460 --> 00:23:53.990
Kai did it!

00:23:53.990 --> 00:23:56.980
Mm-hm. Just as you planned for Q4's strategy?

00:23:56.980 --> 00:24:00.040
Yep! Now you and I must somehow 
make it through, Misaki...

00:24:00.780 --> 00:24:02.420
Tokura Misaki...

00:24:02.420 --> 00:24:04.670
You won't beat me.

00:24:04.670 --> 00:24:08.700
Can you imagine why I'm 
called the "Assassin"?

00:24:08.700 --> 00:24:10.220
Team AL4...

00:24:10.220 --> 00:24:12.270
I wonder how Asaka fights...

00:24:12.270 --> 00:24:14.320
Next time: Beautiful Assassin!

00:24:14.320 --> 00:24:17.250
I'll be two steps ahead of you... 
and I'll win at any cost!
